      "id": 248721,
      "name": "",
      "username": "Thunderbird",
      "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/t/ba8739/{size}.png",
      "created_at": "2022-10-15T02:00:19.687Z",
      "cooked": "<p>I almost always use a sacrificial Tempest and/or LftF/Next Evolution Legacy to avoid the Infernal blast from an environment getting wrecked. OblivAeon’s switching is definitely the worst part of this mode, and hopefully there will be some adjustments come the DE version. You can be all set up to lower a shield, then have your plans trashed by a single ill-timed Scion card that makes him zwoop over to the other side. Oh yeah, and DE incap Tempest is not gonna be the get-outta-nuke-free card anymore. R.I.P.</p>",
